4c7e7295 (Dengnifer 2026-09-04 17:19:42 +0800 1187) 	Induction on the level of $L$. The $0$-level function is the zero function. At level $\ell \ge 1$ we have $L(x) = x^{L_1} + L_{>1,\,x^{L_1}}(x^{V_{>1}})$, where the first summand lies in $V_1 \subseteq S$ and the second lies in $S$ by the induction hypothesis, the factor spaces of $L_{>1,\,x^{L_1}}$ being contained in $S$ as well.
